{"type":"lesson.started","request_id":"1f77503e-5f7e-4a29-ac6e-884952282f95","title":"Integral as area"}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"1f77503e-5f7e-4a29-ac6e-884952282f95","step":{"id":"s1","script":"A definite integral measures signed area between a curve and the horizontal axis. Start with this positive curve from zero to two.","ops":[{"op":"text","id":"title","region":"A1","content":"Integral as signed area"},{"op":"axes","id":"areaaxes","region":"right","x":{"min":0,"max":2.5,"label":"x"},"y":{"min":0,"max":3.5,"label":"y"}},{"op":"curve","id":"function","axes_id":"areaaxes","expr":"x+1","domain":[0,2]},{"op":"equation","id":"target","anchor":{"el":"title","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"\\int_0^2 (x+1)\\,dx"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"1f77503e-5f7e-4a29-ac6e-884952282f95","step":{"id":"s2","script":"Thin rectangles approximate the area. Each rectangle contributes its height times its width; adding them gives an area estimate.","ops":[{"op":"curve","id":"rectangles","axes_id":"areaaxes","expr":"1+0.5*(x-0.25)/sqrt((x-0.25)^2)","domain":[0,0.24]},{"op":"equation","id":"rectangle_area","anchor":{"el":"target","side":"below","gap":0.08},"latex":"\\text{rectangle area}=f(x_i)\\,\\Delta x"},{"op":"equation","id":"sum_area","anchor":{"el":"rectangle_area","side":"below","gap":0.07},"latex":"A\\approx\\sum_{i=1}^{n}f(x_i)\\,\\Delta x"}],"checkpoint":null}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"1f77503e-5f7e-4a29-ac6e-884952282f95","step":{"id":"s3","script":"As rectangle widths shrink toward zero, the sum approaches the definite integral. Here, the region is also a trapezoid.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"limit","anchor":{"el":"sum_area","side":"below","gap":0.07},"latex":"\\int_a^b f(x)\\,dx=\\lim_{n\\to\\infty}\\sum_{i=1}^{n}f(x_i)\\frac{b-a}{n}"},{"op":"equation","id":"exact_area","anchor":{"el":"limit","side":"below","gap":0.07},"latex":"\\int_0^2(x+1)\\,dx=\\frac{1+3}{2}\\cdot2=4"}],"checkpoint":{"question":"Why is this integral positive?","expected_gist":"The curve lies above the horizontal axis on the interval."}}}
{"type":"lesson.step","request_id":"1f77503e-5f7e-4a29-ac6e-884952282f95","step":{"id":"s4","script":"Area above the axis contributes positively; area below contributes negatively. Ordinary geometric area counts both parts positively.","ops":[{"op":"equation","id":"signed","anchor":{"el":"exact_area","side":"below","gap":0.07},"latex":"\\int_a^b f(x)\\,dx=A_{\\text{above}}-A_{\\text{below}}"}],"checkpoint":null}}
